M&T PAM Self-Service and Administrator Rollback

Overview

The M&T PAM Self-Service solution provides an approved and controlled way to temporarily update CyberArk Safe Requestors permissions and, when required, restore those permissions back to their default state.

The solution uses two CyberArk Identity Flows:

PAM Self-Service – used to perform the approved temporary permission change.

Administrator Rollback – used by PAM administrators to restore the affected permissions.

A rollback journal is automatically created for every successfully completed self-service permission change so administrators can clearly identify what remains pending for rollback.

End User Process

An approved user launches the PAM Self-Service application and submits the required request information.

The Flow:

Validates the requested CyberArk Safe and related information.

Identifies the applicable Requestors group.

Applies the approved temporary permission change.

Verifies that the change was successfully completed.

Creates a rollback reference for the PAM administrators.

If the requested change is not successfully verified, no rollback reference is created.

The end user does not need to manually create or manage rollback records.

Administrator Rollback Process

The Administrator Rollback application is restricted to approved PAM administrators.

When launched, the application:

Retrieves all currently pending rollback references.

Displays all available references on one page.

Allows the administrator to select one or multiple references.

Displays the selected references for confirmation.

Restores the applicable Requestors permissions.

Verifies that the rollback was successfully completed.

Removes the completed rollback reference from the pending list.

A rollback reference is only removed after the permissions have been successfully restored and verified.

Rollback Journal

Pending rollback requests are stored in the dedicated CyberArk Safe:

PAM-SELF-SVC-ROLLBACK

The rollback journal contains the information required to identify:

The request / INC reference.

The target CyberArk Safe.

The associated rollback record.

The journal is used only for rollback tracking and does not expose the password of the target managed account.

Administrator Experience

The Administrator Rollback application presents all available pending references in a consolidated list.

Example:

[ ] INC1234567 - AP-ABC-P-C1-AMNG
[ ] INC1234568 - AP-XYZ-P-C1-AMNG
[ ] INC1234569 - AP-WBK-P-C1-AMNG

The administrator may select one or multiple references and process them together.

The application is designed to prevent:

Duplicate rollback processing.

Repeated selection pages.

Processing references that were not selected.

Removing a rollback reference before successful verification.

Permission Restoration

The rollback process restores the applicable Requestors permissions to their standard state.

The Flow preserves the group's other existing CyberArk permissions and changes only the permissions controlled by this self-service process.

Roles and Responsibilities

End Users

End users are responsible for:

Submitting the correct CyberArk Safe and request information.

Providing the approved request or incident reference.

Using the self-service application only for authorized activities.

PAM Administrators

PAM administrators are responsible for:

Reviewing pending rollback references.

Selecting the correct requests for rollback.

Confirming the selected rollback actions.

Investigating any reference that remains pending after a rollback attempt.

Security Controls

The solution includes the following controls:

Only approved users can access the Self-Service application.

Only approved PAM administrators can access Administrator Rollback.

Rollback records are created only after a successful permission change.

Rollback records are removed only after successful rollback verification.

Multiple pending references can be reviewed and processed from one administrator screen.

Duplicate records are not processed more than once.

Target account passwords are not retrieved as part of the rollback process.

CyberArk continues to provide audit visibility for the related Safe and membership changes.

Current Production Baseline

Self-Service Flow

MTB-PAM-Self-Service-Final.json

Administrator Rollback Flow

MTB-PAM-Self-Service-Admin-Rollback-v3-Clean.json

Rollback Safe

PAM-SELF-SVC-ROLLBACK

Rollback Platform

GEN-E-PR0PL0PC0NENR

Expected Result

The completed solution provides a simple lifecycle:

Approved Self-Service Request
        ↓
Temporary Requestors Permission Update
        ↓
Automatic Rollback Reference Created
        ↓
PAM Administrator Reviews Pending Requests
        ↓
Administrator Selects One or More References
        ↓
Permissions Restored
        ↓
Rollback Verified
        ↓
Completed Reference Removed

This provides M&T with a controlled, auditable and repeatable process for managing temporary CyberArk Requestors permissions without requiring administrators to manually track each change.
